PHASE 14: STYLING TOKENS
========================

colors to define
  primary: brand main color
  primary-foreground: text on primary
  secondary: brand secondary
  secondary-foreground: text on secondary
  background: page background
  foreground: main text
  muted: subtle backgrounds
  muted-foreground: subtle text
  accent: highlight color
  accent-foreground: text on accent
  destructive: error color
  border: border color
  ring: focus ring

placeholder color values
  light theme
    background: hsl 0 0% 100%
    foreground: hsl 0 0% 3.9%
    primary: hsl 262 83% 58%
    secondary: hsl 210 40% 96%
    accent: hsl 262 83% 58%
  dark theme
    background: hsl 0 0% 3.9%
    foreground: hsl 0 0% 98%
    primary: hsl 262 83% 68%
    secondary: hsl 215 20% 11%
    accent: hsl 262 83% 68%

---

PHASE 15: RESPONSIVE BREAKPOINTS
================================

breakpoints strategy
  mobile first approach
  base: 0 to 639px mobile
  sm: 640px small tablets
  md: 768px tablets
  lg: 1024px small laptops
  xl: 1280px desktops
  2xl: 1536px large screens

component adjustments
  header
    mobile: hamburger menu
    lg and up: full navigation
  hero
    mobile: stacked, minimal 3d
    md: stacked with 3d
    lg: split layout
  grids
    mobile: single column
    sm: two columns
    lg: three columns
    xl: four columns where needed
  typography
    mobile: smaller sizes
    lg: full sizes
  spacing
    mobile: reduced padding
    lg: full spacing
  3d scenes
    mobile: simplified or hidden
    lg: full complexity

---

PHASE 16: ACCESSIBILITY CHECKLIST
=================================

requirements
  semantic html throughout
  proper heading hierarchy
  alt text for images
  aria labels where needed
  keyboard navigation support
  focus visible styles
  skip to content link
  reduced motion support
  color contrast compliance
  form labels and error messages

implementation notes
  theme toggle: announce to screen readers
  mobile menu: trap focus when open
  animations: respect prefers-reduced-motion
  3d content: provide alternative text content
  interactive elements: minimum 44px touch target

---

PHASE 17: PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS
===================================

next.js
  dynamic imports for heavy components
  image optimization with next/image
  font optimization with next/font
  route prefetching

three.js
  dispose geometries and materials on unmount
  use instancing for repeated objects
  level of detail for complex models
  limit pixel ratio to 2
  use drei performance utilities

animations
  use transform and opacity only
  avoid layout triggering properties
  use will-change sparingly
  debounce scroll handlers
  use requestAnimationFrame

loading
  lazy load below fold sections
  skeleton screens for loading states
  progressive image loading
  preload critical assets

---

PHASE 18: IMPLEMENTATION ORDER
==============================

order of implementation
  1. project setup and dependencies
  2. folder structure creation
  3. configuration files
  4. data files with placeholder content
  5. utility files and constants
  6. custom hooks
  7. providers setup
  8. root layout
  9. common components
  10. layout components header footer
  11. three.js base components
  12. animation components
  13. section components one by one
  14. home page assembly
  15. additional pages
  16. responsive adjustments
  17. accessibility audit
  18. performance optimization

---

NOTES AND REMINDERS
===================

scalability
  all data externalized for easy updates
  components accept data as props
  styles use css variables for theming
  3d scenes can be swapped easily
  sections can be reordered or removed

future additions
  cms integration: data files become api calls
  real images: replace placeholder components
  form handling: add server actions or api routes
  analytics: add tracking provider
  seo: enhance metadata per page
  blog: add blog section with mdx

dependencies to add later if needed
  next-themes: for theme provider
  lenis: alternative smooth scroll
  @studio-freight/lenis: another option
  embla-carousel: for testimonials
  react-hook-form: for forms
  zod: for validation

placeholder images
  use gradient boxes initially
  can use placeholder.com or similar
  replace with real assets when available

testing approach
  each component in isolation first
  then integrate into sections
  then build pages
  test responsive at each step
  test both themes at each step

---

END OF IMPLEMENTATION PLAN
